Portions of this project are adapted from NeMo-Speech.cpp
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Speech.cpp),
Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

  - cmake/materialize_llama_cpp.cmake: llama.cpp patch application, adapted
    from cmake/llama_cpp.cmake.
  - nemo_speech/models.py: model catalog, cache layout and ranged tokenizer
    download, ported from app/model_store.cpp.
  - nemo_speech/capi/*.py: ctypes declarations mirroring include/nemo_speech/*.h.

patches/llama.cpp/ contains modifications to llama.cpp
(https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
authors, licensed under the MIT License.

Binary distributions (wheels) bundle NeMo-Speech.cpp, ggml/llama.cpp,
SentencePiece, Open JTalk with MeCab and the NAIST Japanese Dictionary
(compiled), cppjieba with limonp, NeMo-Speech.cpp's Mandarin G2P tables
(generated from Jieba, pypinyin and pypinyin-dict) and, depending on the
platform, compiler runtime libraries:
Linux wheels bundle libgomp (GCC's OpenMP runtime; GPL-3.0 with the GCC
Runtime Library Exception 3.1), and Windows wheels the Microsoft Visual C++
runtime (Visual Studio Distributable Code). Their license texts and notices
are included in the package under nemo_speech/licenses/.

CUDA wheels additionally bundle the NVIDIA CUDA Runtime, cuBLAS and cuBLASLt
libraries. They are NVIDIA redistributables provided under the NVIDIA CUDA
Toolkit End User License Agreement (nemo_speech/licenses/third_party/cuda/
EULA.txt), are not covered by the Apache License, and are used only by this
package.

Models are not distributed with this project. nemo_speech.models downloads
them on request from their publishers; they are governed by their own licenses,
which you are responsible for reviewing and complying with.
